WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.123 --> 00:00:02.195
- Hey, I'm Kelly and I like warm hugs.

00:00:02.195 --> 00:00:03.340
(laughing)

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.360
That's why I hugged you.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.437
- That's supposed to
be my line, but go on.

00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:07.900
- No, I wanted to steal it
before you could say it.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.733
That's who I am.

00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:10.840
- I feel like I have competition now

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.672
and I'm not happy about
it but that's okay.

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:13.505
(laughing)

00:00:13.505 --> 00:00:14.880
- Well welcome to ambush Christmas.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:15.713
- Thank you so much.

00:00:15.713 --> 00:00:17.140
- Do you like Christmas as much as this?

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.590
- No I love Christmas.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.721
So I'm the guy who,

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:23.060
Halloween stops and the
next day I call somebody

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.710
to start putting the Christmas lights

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.490
'cause I'm incapable of climbing trees

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.323
and putting Christmas lights.

00:00:27.323 --> 00:00:28.156
(laughing)

00:00:28.156 --> 00:00:30.755
I will say that, I'm Jewish,
you can applaud that.

00:00:30.755 --> 00:00:31.697
(laughing)

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.031
(audience applauding)

00:00:33.031 --> 00:00:34.514
Yes!

00:00:34.514 --> 00:00:36.078
We did it!

00:00:36.078 --> 00:00:37.010
- We did it!

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:38.630
- Christmas is such a novelty for me.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:40.885
My wife is Catholic.

00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:41.718
And you know growing up,

00:00:41.718 --> 00:00:44.610
on Christmas for us we
would get Chinese food

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.470
and watch "The Goonies" for the 50th time.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.180
- Okay well, "The Goonies" is amazing.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.466
- It's amazing, but that's no
way to celebrate Christmas.

00:00:50.466 --> 00:00:51.299
- Maybe not.

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:52.140
- That's just a Wednesday night.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.430
So I was like dying to actually

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:56.868
start Christmas like, immediately.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.780
And then I made my wife
go to midnight mass

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.207
because I love it so much.

00:01:01.207 --> 00:01:03.070
I'm like can they do that stuff

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.380
where they sing again in Latin?

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.425
That's the coolest thing ever.

00:01:05.425 --> 00:01:07.730
And like, I will drag her.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.550
I love it so much, so I
just love the holiday.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.383
- I love it too.

00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:12.216
It's just so happy.

00:01:12.216 --> 00:01:13.049
It's just a happy, happy time of year.

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:14.320
- It is so happy.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.270
- Well Thanksgiving is tomorrow,

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.700
do you celebrate big on that too?

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.739
I do celebrate, clearly.

00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:18.572
(laughing)

00:01:18.572 --> 00:01:20.161
- Clearly I do too.

00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:21.000
Clearly I'm all in.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.414
- I love Thanksgiving so much.

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:25.080
My wife has this cousin
Monique who literally,

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.095
this is not an exaggeration,

00:01:26.095 --> 00:01:27.119
she talks like this,

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.924
guys, so good to see you.

00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:30.661
Welcome to the house, how are you?

00:01:30.661 --> 00:01:32.280
Welcome to Thanksgiving.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.490
- Possibly a smoker?

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.768
- Yeah, possibly a smoker,

00:01:34.768 --> 00:01:36.831
possibly a character in "The Incredibles,"

00:01:36.831 --> 00:01:38.037
but definitely.

00:01:38.037 --> 00:01:39.119
(laughing)

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:42.730
This woman, and so she does
the most insane Thanksgiving

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:43.977
in Washington, D.C. every year

00:01:43.977 --> 00:01:46.791
and she basically has six turkeys.

00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:47.777
- What?

00:01:47.777 --> 00:01:48.750
- Yes.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.967
Not like living turkeys.

00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:51.484
Like, just prepared turkeys.

00:01:51.484 --> 00:01:53.692
So she's got, a cajun turkey.

00:01:53.692 --> 00:01:54.820
- Oh that looks good.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:55.653
Oh there we go!

00:01:55.653 --> 00:01:56.486
Oh I want it!

00:01:56.486 --> 00:01:57.489
I want it now!

00:01:57.489 --> 00:01:58.322
(laughing)

00:01:58.322 --> 00:02:00.160
And so we go there and we have this meal

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.040
and it's like that scene in
"Raiders of the Lost Ark"

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.840
that melts your face when you just see

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.500
this smorgasbord of food out there.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.630
Yes, yes!

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.463
- I'm the same way.

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:11.020
As long as there has to be gravy

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:12.092
on the table or I'm leaving.

00:02:12.092 --> 00:02:12.950
- Always gravy.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:13.783
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:13.783 --> 00:02:15.460
- You need to put the
gravy on the stuffing,

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:16.647
stuffing on the turkey,

00:02:16.647 --> 00:02:18.190
all of it in my mouth.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.472
- In one magical bite.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.380
(applause)

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:21.900
What did your daughters
think of "Frozen 2?"

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.970
They've seen it obviously, right?

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:23.803
- They saw it.

00:02:23.803 --> 00:02:26.960
They absolutely freaked out.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:27.793
Loved it.

00:02:27.793 --> 00:02:28.626
- Aw!

00:02:28.626 --> 00:02:30.670
You're like the coolest dad ever to them!

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.789
- No, usually they're not fans of me.

00:02:32.789 --> 00:02:33.711
(laughing)

00:02:33.711 --> 00:02:37.768
With this movie when they
saw this, my oldest one looks

00:02:37.768 --> 00:02:40.876
at me through like gritted
teeth and she goes,

00:02:40.876 --> 00:02:43.084
"When can I see it again?

00:02:43.084 --> 00:02:45.155
(laughing)

00:02:45.155 --> 00:02:47.540
"I liked it more than the first one."

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.373
I'm like thanks,

00:02:48.373 --> 00:02:49.529
I didn't ask you for your
review but thank you.

00:02:49.529 --> 00:02:51.287
(laughing)

00:02:51.287 --> 00:02:53.140
- The kids will give you their review.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.397
- Kids will give you their review.

00:02:54.397 --> 00:02:55.230
- Yes they will.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.063
- Like what was the alternative?

00:02:56.063 --> 00:02:57.400
Mm, hated that one.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.419
(laughing)

00:02:58.419 --> 00:03:01.238
Is there still time to re-record, daddy?

00:03:01.238 --> 00:03:02.470
- Can you fix that?

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.380
- Can you fix that scene?

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.711
- My mom does that with this show.

00:03:04.711 --> 00:03:05.961
- The Samantha joke didn't track for me.

00:03:05.961 --> 00:03:06.794
(laughing)

00:03:06.794 --> 00:03:07.627
- My mother does that this show,

00:03:07.627 --> 00:03:08.781
"Maybe you should put
your chair in the middle."

00:03:08.781 --> 00:03:09.851
(laughing)

00:03:09.851 --> 00:03:12.430
Mom, there's a reason
why we did it this way.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:13.263
I love her, she's great.

00:03:13.263 --> 00:03:16.850
I actually ruined
"Frozen" for my daughter.

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:17.940
So when I did "UglyDolls,"

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:18.773
it's an animated film,

00:03:18.773 --> 00:03:19.710
I was like yeah, you know,

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.040
like Mommy's the voice of Moxy

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.995
like you know how Elsa, the real singer,

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:25.092
and I started telling her.

00:03:25.092 --> 00:03:28.340
As I'm saying it, I just saw--

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.270
